{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>וְהֵשִׁיב אֶת אֲשָׁמוֹ.</b> It changed to speak in the singular, even though it began to speak in the plural — ״וְהִתְוַדּוּ״ — for the confessions are all equal in him, which is not so with the guilt-offering, which is not uniform, for it varies upward and downward as stated in parashat Vayikra (Leviticus 5:7–13). And the verse finished speaking of this measure in the singular, for there is no need to vary and write in a different manner."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:12.290196935Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}